From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:02:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally bound the host window
 check

Every poll pass and every submission checks the host window: it reads
back, uncached, every linked entry of the shared L2 of the 64 GiB host
window, one entry per 32 MiB. An entry is linked the first time anything
is mapped in its 32 MiB and is never unlinked, because its L3 table is
never freed. The objects in it are freed and their VA reused, but the
link stays. So the check's length is the most host-window VA the boot
has ever used, which grows with every client mix (overlapping clients,
arenas held by unit leases, fragmentation of the best-fit allocator) and
never shrinks. A light compute command gets slower the more clients the
boot has run.

Add aurora.g16_window_check_n (runtime, default 0: unchanged). With N > 0
a check still verifies the firmware root words, then reads N linked
shared-L2 words round robin from a list of the linked indices, which is
rebuilt only after a new link. Every linked word is still read at least
once every ceil(linked / N) checks, and linking a new entry (sync_range)
still compares all 2048 words. The choice of words is in g16/winscan.rs
with host tests.

The stats file reports "window: linked L check_n N bounded_checks C
bounded_words W", so the growth itself can be read off.

Assisted-by: LLM
